EDIT 1 (main fix) — add a helper in /workspace/src/chart/bar/BarView.ts immediately after `createPolarPositionMapping` (which ends at line 1000) and before `function updateStyle` (line 1002):
```ts
/**
 * `layout.width` / `layout.height` can be exactly 0 when the value equals the value
 * axis start value. In that case its sign can not tell which side is "outside", and it
 * used to fall back to 'bottom'/'right' regardless of the axis direction.
 * Use the direction that a positive value grows to instead, which is decided by the
 * `inverse` of the value axis. (Same rule as `pxSign` in PictorialBarView.)
 */
function getCartesianLabelPositionOutside(
    coordSys: Cartesian2D,
    layout: RectLayout,
    isBaseHorizontal: boolean
): 'top' | 'bottom' | 'left' | 'right' {
    const valueAxis = coordSys.getOtherAxis(coordSys.getBaseAxis());
    // The value axis is vertical when the base (category) axis is horizontal.
    const isValueAxisX = !isBaseHorizontal;
    const isInverse = valueAxis.inverse;
    const size = isBaseHorizontal ? layout.height : layout.width;
    const sign = (isValueAxisX && !isInverse) || (!isValueAxisX && isInverse)
        ? (size >= 0 ? 1 : -1)
        : (size > 0 ? 1 : -1);
    return isBaseHorizontal
        ? (sign > 0 ? 'bottom' : 'top')
        : (sign > 0 ? 'right' : 'left');
}
```
No new imports are required: `Cartesian2D` is already imported as a type at BarView.ts:56, `RectLayout` is the local alias declared at line 81. `Cartesian2D.getBaseAxis(): Axis2D` (/workspace/src/coord/cartesian/Cartesian2D.ts:90) and `getOtherAxis(axis: Axis2D): Axis2D` (:175) exist, and `Axis.inverse` is declared at /workspace/src/coord/Axis.ts:81.

